   "body": "## Goal\nReport, do not fix: establish whether one meaningful VI logic change is supported by available evidence before ordering the disk edit. Expected gain is docs/research/poc/edit-readiness.md and edit-readiness.json containing either one executable edit recipe with evidence or a bounded negative finding and possible exits. The next shaper reads the edit-readiness verdict to order an edit or deliver a documented POC failure. Existing README establishes full heap framing but explicitly leaves primitive meaning, integrity and compiled-cache consistency unresolved. No session can run LabVIEW; opening, behavior and runtime validity remain owner checks.\n\n## Work\n1. Reuse inspect_vi.py and the saved grammar. Do not repeat RSRC/decompression/framing research. Search the pinned source snapshots and their provenance for a primitive identity/replacement contract, constant encoding, BDPW integrity and compiled-code invalidation rules. Check whether LVparts-source.txt actually contains the relevant classes; a missing match is not proof that the format has no integrity rule. If a missing source is retrieved through permitted tools, pin its URL, revision, license and hash.\n2. Prefer the smallest demonstrable semantic change. Either substantiate a compatible primitive replacement independently of the add.vi filename, or inspect at most 12 small public fixtures for a typed numeric/Boolean/string constant that contributes to logic. Names and raw integers alone are not semantic evidence. Do not assume 103 -> 104 means Add -> Subtract. Record fixture selection criteria, inspected paths/hashes and failures; no bulk dump of the actor-framework corpus.\n3. For the selected route, document node/terminal connectivity, field type/value and exact original-byte spans, intended before/after meaning, evidence for the replacement, container rebuild requirements, applicable integrity updates and compiled-cache handling. Distinguish source-derived rules, byte observations and h